        {% endfor %}
      {% else %}
        {% for i in (1..4) %}
          {% case i %}
            {% when 1 %}
              {% assign chc_step_number = 'Step 01' %}
              {% assign chc_step_headline = 'Position along the gumline.' %}
              {% capture chc_step_body %}<p>Hold the FlowCore nozzle at a 90° angle to your teeth, tip touching the gumline. This is the entry angle for subgingival access, the zone 2 to 6mm below the tissue surface where bacteria accumulate and where a toothbrush physically cannot reach.</p>{% endcapture %}
              {% assign chc_callout_text = 'Correct nozzle angle reduces resistance and allows the precision stream to enter the sulcus at full pressure.' %}
              {% assign chc_cta_label = blank %}
              {% assign chc_cta_link = blank %}
              {% assign chc_cta_style = 'navy' %}
              {% assign chc_annotation_type = 'angle' %}
              {% assign chc_image_alt = 'FlowCore positioned at 90 degree angle along the gumline' %}
            {% when 2 %}
              {% assign chc_step_number = 'Step 02' %}
              {% assign chc_step_headline = 'Penetrate 6mm below the gumline.' %}
              {% capture chc_step_body %}<p>The 0.6mm precision stream enters the space between tooth and gum tissue, reaching up to 6mm subgingivally. String floss reaches approximately 2 to 3mm. At 1,600 pulses per minute, the stream creates a hydrodynamic zone that physically disrupts biofilm, the bacterial layer that causes plaque and gum inflammation.</p>{% endcapture %}
              {% assign chc_callout_text = 'String floss maximum penetration: 2–3mm. FlowCore subgingival reach: up to 6mm. The difference is where periodontal disease begins.' %}
              {% assign chc_cta_label = blank %}
              {% assign chc_cta_link = blank %}
              {% assign chc_cta_style = 'navy' %}
              {% assign chc_annotation_type = 'stream' %}
              {% assign chc_image_alt = 'FlowCore nozzle tip close-up with water stream entering between teeth' %}
            {% when 3 %}
              {% assign chc_step_number = 'Step 03' %}
              {% assign chc_step_headline = 'Flush out the biofilm barrier.' %}
              {% capture chc_step_body %}<p>Plaque is not just food debris, it is a structured bacterial community called biofilm. Biofilm resists manual removal and blocks nano-HA from bonding to enamel. The FlowCore's pulsating stream physically breaks up and flushes biofilm from interdental spaces and below the gumline, clearing access for remineralisation.</p>{% endcapture %}
              {% assign chc_callout_text = '99.9% plaque removal in clinical testing versus brushing alone. Journal of Clinical Dentistry, 2019.' %}
              {% assign chc_cta_label = blank %}
              {% assign chc_cta_link = blank %}
              {% assign chc_cta_style = 'navy' %}
              {% assign chc_annotation_type = 'particles' %}
              {% assign chc_image_alt = 'FlowCore flushing plaque debris from between teeth' %}
            {% else %}
